Fri Oct 16 08:25:18 AM UTC 2026
$PROBLEM ferx #1082 design anchor -- 3 nested levels, exact (IOV-style) coding
; ID = SPONSOR (top level). Below it: STUDY (2 per sponsor, unweighted) and
; ARM (2 per study, weighted gamma^2/NARM), coded as occasion-style ETA slots
; with $OMEGA SAME. Per-sponsor likelihood is independent => ordinary FOCEI.
$INPUT ID STUDY ARM ARMID=DROP STUDYID=DROP SLOT TIME DV NARM DOSE
$DATA nested_levels_3.csv IGNORE=@
$PRED
  EST = 0
  IF(STUDY.EQ.1) EST = ETA(2)
  IF(STUDY.EQ.2) EST = ETA(3)
  KAR = 0
  IF(SLOT.EQ.1) KAR = ETA(4)
  IF(SLOT.EQ.2) KAR = ETA(5)
  IF(SLOT.EQ.3) KAR = ETA(6)
  IF(SLOT.EQ.4) KAR = ETA(7)
  EMAX = THETA(2)*EXP(ETA(1) + EST + KAR/SQRT(NARM))
  IPRED = THETA(1) + EMAX*DOSE/(THETA(3)+DOSE)*TIME/(TIME+THETA(4))
  Y = IPRED + EPS(1)
$THETA (0, 10) (0, 20) (0.1, 30) (0.01, 3)
$OMEGA 0.09            ; ETA(1) sponsor
$OMEGA BLOCK(1) 0.04   ; ETA(2) study slot 1
$OMEGA BLOCK(1) SAME   ; ETA(3) study slot 2
$OMEGA BLOCK(1) 4      ; ETA(4) arm slot 1 (unweighted gamma^2)
$OMEGA BLOCK(1) SAME
$OMEGA BLOCK(1) SAME
$OMEGA BLOCK(1) SAME
$SIGMA 0.25
$ESTIMATION METHOD=1 INTER MAXEVAL=9999 PRINT=5 NOABORT SIGDIG=4
$COVARIANCE MATRIX=R
$TABLE ID STUDY SLOT TIME IPRED ETA1 ETA2 ETA3 ETA4 ETA5 ETA6 ETA7 NOPRINT NOAPPEND ONEHEADER FORMAT=s1PE15.8 FILE=nested_levels_3.tab

NM-TRAN MESSAGES
  
 WARNINGS AND ERRORS (IF ANY) FOR PROBLEM    1
             
 (WARNING  2) NM-TRAN INFERS THAT THE DATA ARE POPULATION.
             
 (WARNING  13) WITH USER-WRITTEN PRED OR $PRED, NM-TRAN CANNOT APPEND THE
 MDV DATA ITEM.
  
Note: Analytical 2nd Derivatives are constructed in FSUBS but are never used.
      You may insert $ABBR DERIV2=NO after the first $PROB to save FSUBS construction and compilation time
  

